            <ArticleTitle>Preferential utilization of free cholesterol from high-density lipoproteins for biliary cholesterol secretion in man.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>62-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>High- and low-density lipoproteins carrying free cholesterol labeled with 3H or 14C were administered to a patient with a bile fistula. The free cholesterol from high-density lipoproteins was more rapidly incorporated into biliary cholesterol than the free cholesterol from low-density lipoproteins. These findings show that the liver in man selectively utilizes and secretes the free cholesterol from a particular lipoprotein.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
